1
00:00:08,908 --> 00:00:17,469
-==www.RagBear.com==- 是, 首相  第1季第3集

2
00:00:18,515 --> 00:00:23,031
<font color="#4096d1">本字幕仅供学习交流，严禁用于商业用途

3
00:00:23,031 --> 00:00:32,129
<font color="#4096d1">-=破烂熊字幕组=- 翻译: ethanzdp 校对&时间轴: tpring

4
00:00:37,078 --> 00:00:41,379
烟幕重重

5
00:00:41,571 --> 00:00:44,767
弗兰克 问题是 凡是新首相
Frank, the problem is all new Prime Ministers

6
00:00:44,767 --> 00:00:46,731
都想削减税收 或者公共支出
want to cut either taxes or public expenditure.

7
00:00:46,766 --> 00:00:49,199
谢谢 这也是哈克想干的事
Thank you. That's what Hacker wants, too.

8
00:00:49,371 --> 00:00:51,441
政客就和孩子一样
Politicians are like children.

9
00:00:51,611 --> 00:00:55,320
不能让他们为所欲为 否则会宠坏他们      对
give them what they want only encourages them!

10
00:00:55,491 --> 00:00:58,244
但是 有一点要明确 汉弗莱
But let's be clear about this, Humphrey.

11
00:00:58,851 --> 00:01:03,242
整个体制要靠你这个内阁秘书来控制首相
The entire system hinges on you as Cabinet Secretary controlling the PM

12
00:01:03,411 --> 00:01:07,643
我这个财政部常任秘书控制财政大臣
and on me as Permanent Secretary at the Treasury controlling the Chancellor.

13
00:01:07,811 --> 00:01:09,369
是吧?      是
Right? Right.

14
00:01:09,531 --> 00:01:14,241
还要我们保持他们关系紧张 猜忌 敌对
And on both of us keeping an agreeable tension between them, mistrust, hostility.

15
00:01:14,451 --> 00:01:18,239
放心吧 没有我们 他俩也不会太热乎
Mind you, I think they'd manage that all right even without us.

16
00:01:18,411 --> 00:01:23,405
财政大臣永不会原谅首相打败他进入了10号
The Chancellor will never forgive the Prime Minister for beating him to Number 10

17
00:01:23,571 --> 00:01:26,722
而首相 他永远也不会相信财政大臣
and the Prime Minister will never trust the Chancellor.

18
00:01:26,891 --> 00:01:30,520
毕竟 你不能信任你骗过的人     也许不能
One never trusts anyone one has deceived. Perhaps not.

19
00:01:30,691 --> 00:01:33,763
减税能让他们齐心协力 会给他俩都赢得选票
But tax cuts unite them. They get them both votes.

20
00:01:33,971 --> 00:01:38,761
对 可是弗兰克 这次减税得靠首相幻想的
Yes, but surely this tax cut is contingent upon the Prime Minister's fantasy

21
00:01:38,931 --> 00:01:42,321
取消三叉戟 重振陆军的计划吧
about cancelling Trident and switching to conventional forces.

22
00:01:42,531 --> 00:01:47,161
反正 他想拱手让出15亿我们的钱
Nevertheless, he is giving away ?.5 billion of our money!

23
00:01:47,331 --> 00:01:50,656
不可想象 提案也不行
It's unthinkable, even if only proposals.

24
00:01:50,656 --> 00:01:53,500
我费了好大劲说服财政大臣反对它
I had a real job getting the Chancellor to oppose it.

25
00:01:53,535 --> 00:01:54,962
你怎么做的?
How did you do it?

26
00:01:55,131 --> 00:01:59,761
我说我们需要钱资助医院 学校和老人
I used the one about our needing the money for hospitals, schools and old people.

27
00:01:59,931 --> 00:02:02,923
人工肾战术     对 "人道主义大臣"
The kidney machine gambit. The caring Chancellor (!)

28
00:02:03,131 --> 00:02:05,599
就是这个办法     是啊 这招是管用
Yes, that one. It usually works.

29
00:02:05,771 --> 00:02:08,259
可是弗兰克 减点税不用这么小题大做吧?
But would a tax cut matter all that much?

30
00:02:08,259 --> 00:02:10,099
只是15亿而已
It's only ?.5 billion.

31
00:02:10,451 --> 00:02:15,366
对 钱是不多 我是担心你居然让它轻易通过了
I agree, it's not much in itself. My worry is about you letting it get through so soon.

32
00:02:16,931 --> 00:02:19,445
如果我是你们财政部秘书
If I were in your shoes at the Treasury,

33
00:02:19,611 --> 00:02:24,366
我会更担心现在的经济状况 低生产力
I'd be much more worried about the state of the economy, low productivity.

34
00:02:25,371 --> 00:02:27,407
这可不是我们的错
That's not our fault.

35
00:02:27,571 --> 00:02:31,803
都怪英国工人 好吃懒做 就想天上掉馅饼
It's the British worker fundamentally lazy, wants something for nothing.

36
00:02:31,971 --> 00:02:34,704
旷工时数越来越多
The figures for absenteeism are going up and up.

37
00:02:34,704 --> 00:02:36,687
没人肯老实工作一天
Nobody wants to do an honest day's work.

38
00:02:37,222 --> 00:02:39,804
真惊人 总之 我得走了     下午很忙?
Shocking! I must rush. Busy afternoon?

39
00:02:40,011 --> 00:02:42,650
是啊 我听说英格兰是3比70
Yes, indeed. I gather England are 70 for 3.

40
00:02:51,131 --> 00:02:53,520
喔 喔 慢点 杰拉德
Whoa, whoa! Easy does it, Gerald.

41
00:02:53,731 --> 00:02:57,963
这种酒多得是      干杯 敬公务员系统
Plenty more where that came from. Cheers. To the Civil Service!

42
00:02:58,851 --> 00:03:01,490
敬英国的烟草集团及其主席
To the British Tobacco Group and its chairman.

43
00:03:01,651 --> 00:03:03,642
谢谢
Thank you.

44
00:03:06,291 --> 00:03:08,805
一下午板球真惬意啊
I do love a good afternoon's cricket.

45
00:03:10,531 --> 00:03:14,524
知道吗 你们烟草集团的人都是国家的恩人
You know, you chaps at BTG are national benefactors really.

46
00:03:14,691 --> 00:03:16,682
您这么想 我真的非常荣幸
We like to think so.

47
00:03:16,851 --> 00:03:22,323
杰拉德 我想请你帮个忙 给皇家歌剧院
You know, Gerald, I've got a small favour to ask on behalf of the Royal Opera House.

48
00:03:22,491 --> 00:03:27,007
你知道 伦敦剧院区差不多是为内阁运营的
Now, as you know, Covent Garden is more or less run from the Cabinet Office.

49
00:03:27,891 --> 00:03:33,523
但我听说 明年有些剧目要难产了 资金不足
But I'm told that one or more productions are threatened next year, lack of funds.

50
00:03:33,731 --> 00:03:37,565
今天下午我请了体育大臣来
Well, I've got the Minister for Sport coming along this afternoon.

51
00:03:37,731 --> 00:03:41,331
我知道他想拉我支援温布尔登
I know he wants to twist my arm on behalf of Wimbledon

52
00:03:41,331 --> 00:03:42,870
布兰兹哈奇赛车之类的
or Brands Hatch or something.

53
00:03:42,891 --> 00:03:45,485
伦敦剧院区...我们想想办法
Covent Garden... We'll see what we can do.

54
00:03:45,651 --> 00:03:48,643
哦 要是没有你 我们都该怎么办呢?
Oh, I don't know where we'd all be without you.

55
00:03:49,251 --> 00:03:51,765
告诉我 你请了彼得索恩吗?
Tell me, have you ever invited Peter Thorne?

56
00:03:51,931 --> 00:03:55,128
卫生大臣?      是 你总得顾及他的
The Minister of Health? You always included them.

57
00:03:55,331 --> 00:03:58,528
他来不了 被禁烟游说团拉去了
This one's been got at by the anti-smoking lobby.

58
00:03:58,731 --> 00:04:00,801
哦 多愚蠢的人啊
Oh, silly man!

59
00:04:01,011 --> 00:04:04,799
非常蠢 他在政府里影响不大吧?
Very silly. He hasn't got much clout in Whitehall, has he?

60
00:04:05,011 --> 00:04:07,241
无足轻重 他只是个大臣嘛
None at all. He's just a minister.

61
00:04:08,491 --> 00:04:10,482
好球
Good shot!

62
00:04:12,171 --> 00:04:14,162
他出局了?
Was he out?

63
00:04:15,051 --> 00:04:19,488
汉弗莱 这份报告上说 如果以征兵取代三叉戟
Humphrey, this paper says that if we cancel Trident and bring in conscription,

64
00:04:19,651 --> 00:04:22,961
我们可以减税15亿 可你猜我发现什么?
we shall have ?.5 billion for tax cuts, and what do I find?

65
00:04:23,171 --> 00:04:27,164
您发现什么 首相?     我发现财政大臣竟然反对
What do you find, Prime Minister? The Chancellor opposes me.

66
00:04:27,331 --> 00:04:32,121
这是多好的挣选票机会 他却不要 你不惊讶吗?
A great chance to be popular with the voters and he says no. Doesn't that surprise you?

67
00:04:32,331 --> 00:04:33,923
不惊讶
No.

68
00:04:34,411 --> 00:04:36,561
我倒是吃了一惊 你怎么这么平静?
Why doesn't it surprise you?

69
00:04:36,771 --> 00:04:40,889
他听财政部的 他们吃进的钱可不会吐出来
He's advised by the Treasury and they don't believe in giving money back.

70
00:04:41,051 --> 00:04:43,555
又不是他们的 是纳税人的钱
It's not theirs. It's the taxpayers'.

71
00:04:43,555 --> 00:04:45,649
是有这么一说 可财政部不同意
That's not the view the Treasury takes.

72
00:04:46,131 --> 00:04:49,487
只要钱入了他们掌控     可如果他们不需要
Not once they've got it. But if they don't need it?

73
00:04:49,651 --> 00:04:52,529
什么?     如果他们不需要
Sorry? If they don't need it.

74
00:04:52,691 --> 00:04:56,479
税收和需求无关     那和什么有关?
Taxation isn't about what you need. What is it about?

75
00:04:56,651 --> 00:05:02,726
首相 财政部不会先想好怎么花 再设法敛财
The Treasury doesn't work out what they need and then think how to raise the money.

76
00:05:02,931 --> 00:05:04,922
那他们怎么做?
What DOES it do?

77
00:05:05,091 --> 00:05:10,085
只要可能 敛得越多越好 然后再找地方花
They pitch for as much as they can get away with, then think what to spend it on.

78
00:05:10,691 --> 00:05:14,001
如果因为不需要 就把钱还回去
If you start giving money back because you don't need it,

79
00:05:14,171 --> 00:05:17,004
您就破坏了几个世纪的老规矩
you're breaking with centuries of tradition.

80
00:05:17,171 --> 00:05:20,220
比如 英国海军会怎么样?
What would happen to the British Navy?

81
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:22,055
照旧 我们需要海军嘛
We still need a navy.

82
00:05:22,090 --> 00:05:25,316
我们只有4艘大型军舰 所以只需4个海军上将
We have four capital ships, so we need only four admirals

83
00:05:25,316 --> 00:05:27,231
和1个元帅就够了
and one Admiral of the Fleet.

84
00:05:27,266 --> 00:05:29,369
现在有多少上将?     60个
How many Admirals have we got? 60.

85
00:05:30,451 --> 00:05:34,239
财政部是最有权势的部 因为它控制所有的钱
The Treasury's the most powerful department as it controls all the money.

86
00:05:34,411 --> 00:05:38,165
夺走它的钱 等于夺走它的权 他们自然要反抗
If you take away its money, you take away its power, so they resist.

87
00:05:38,371 --> 00:05:42,569
那怎样让财政部同意减税?     让财政大臣同意
How will the Treasury agree to tax cuts? Get the Chancellor to agree.

88
00:05:42,771 --> 00:05:45,843
怎样才能让大臣同意呢?     让财政部同意
How will the Chancellor agree? Get the Treasury to agree.

89
00:05:46,051 --> 00:05:49,680
汉弗莱 这不可能     对 首相 这本来就不可能
This is impossible. Yes, Prime Minister, it is impossible.

90
00:05:49,891 --> 00:05:54,646
一定有办法逼财政部出手     有啊 逼大臣出手
We must be able to force the Treasury's hand. Yes, by forcing the Chancellor's hand.

91
00:05:54,851 --> 00:05:58,685
怎么逼大臣出手呢?     逼财政部出手
How do I force the Chancellor's hand? By forcing the Treasury's hand.

92
00:05:58,891 --> 00:06:01,320
汉弗莱      首相 您不能说服财政大臣吗?
Can't YOU persuade the Chancellor?

93
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,642
他毕竟是您的内阁成员
He's your Cabinet colleague.

94
00:06:02,642 --> 00:06:06,000
关键就在这里 我需要有个自己人帮忙
That's the point. I need help from somebody who's on my side.

95
00:06:07,131 --> 00:06:09,599
首相 卫生部大臣来了
The Minister of State at the DHSS is here.

96
00:06:09,771 --> 00:06:13,400
让他进来 谢谢 汉弗莱      谢谢 首相
Show him in. Thank you, Humphrey. Thank you, Prime Minister.

97
00:06:13,571 --> 00:06:16,563
索恩博士 首相      彼得 快进来
Dr Thorne, Prime Minister. Peter, come in.

98
00:06:17,611 --> 00:06:19,602
请坐
Sit down.

99
00:06:19,771 --> 00:06:22,683
你想跟我讨论...?
Now, you wanted to talk to me about...?

100
00:06:23,611 --> 00:06:26,205
香烟     哦 对对
Cigarettes. Ah, yes.

101
00:06:26,371 --> 00:06:29,329
您看我的报告了吧?     那是当然
You read my paper? Yes, absolutely.

102
00:06:29,491 --> 00:06:31,686
您作何感想?
How did you react?

103
00:06:31,851 --> 00:06:35,560
好的 你能否用自己的话总结一下呢?
Well, I...wonder if you could summarise it in your own words.

104
00:06:38,051 --> 00:06:40,690
这就是我自己的话
Those WERE my own words.

105
00:06:41,371 --> 00:06:44,044
是 当然 当然
Yes, yes, exactly, of course.

106
00:06:44,251 --> 00:06:49,803
但首相一向认为 摘要可以明确要点 概括重点
But the Prime Minister often finds that a brief summary focuses on the salient points.

107
00:06:49,971 --> 00:06:52,360
重点 没错
Salient points, precisely.

108
00:06:53,411 --> 00:06:58,405
好 简而言之 我提议政府采取行动来禁烟
Well, briefly, I'm proposing that the government should take action to eliminate smoking,

109
00:06:58,571 --> 00:07:02,325
彻底封杀对烟草的赞助和广告 甚至销售
a complete ban on all cigarette sponsorship and advertising,

110
00:07:02,531 --> 00:07:05,887
投入5千万宣传禁烟政策
?0 million to be spent on anti-smoking publicity,

111
00:07:06,051 --> 00:07:11,171
所有公共场所禁烟 未来5年内提高烟草累进税
a ban on smoking in all public places and progressive tax rises over the next five years

112
00:07:11,331 --> 00:07:15,119
直到一包20根的烟和一瓶威士忌一样贵
until a packet of 20 costs about the same as a bottle of whisky.

113
00:07:17,171 --> 00:07:19,446
这是不是太猛了点?
Isn't that rather drastic?

114
00:07:19,651 --> 00:07:23,561
当然 这样能减少80%吸烟率
Absolutely. It should reduce smoking by at least 80%

115
00:07:23,561 --> 00:07:25,157
走运的话能减少90%
90% if we're lucky

116
00:07:25,157 --> 00:07:27,291
能让所有烟草公司破产
and drive tobacco companies out of business.

117
00:07:28,131 --> 00:07:32,568
当然 彼得 你知道基本上我是支持你的
Yes. Well, Peter, of course, you know I agree with you basically.

118
00:07:32,731 --> 00:07:35,086
吸烟理应被禁止
Smoking should be stopped.

119
00:07:35,251 --> 00:07:38,323
毫无疑问 我们终归要完成这项任务
No question. And we will stop it in due course.

120
00:07:39,211 --> 00:07:42,681
等时机成熟 万事俱备
At the appropriate juncture, in the fullness of time.

121
00:07:43,771 --> 00:07:46,763
您是说算了?     当然不是
You mean forget it? No, absolutely not.

122
00:07:47,811 --> 00:07:51,201
但我们得现实些 你我都不是昨天刚出生
But we must be realists. You and I weren't born yesterday.

123
00:07:51,411 --> 00:07:55,040
对 也不是昨天刚死掉      什么?
No, and we didn't die yesterday. No. What?

124
00:07:56,131 --> 00:08:00,727
每天有300人因吸烟英年早逝
300 people did prematurely as a result of smoking.

125
00:08:00,891 --> 00:08:03,769
每年至少10万人死亡
100,000 deaths a year at least.

126
00:08:03,971 --> 00:08:07,218
的确吓人 但你知道内阁会怎么说
It's appalling, but you know

127
00:08:07,218 --> 00:08:08,195
财政部会怎么说?
what the Treasury would say?

128
00:08:08,230 --> 00:08:12,483
对 他们会说烟草每年带来40亿税收 至关重要
They'd say that smoking brings in ? billion a year in revenue.

129
00:08:12,691 --> 00:08:16,445
你斗不过财务部的      对 从财政方面而言
You can't beat the Treasury. Not with financial arguments.

130
00:08:16,611 --> 00:08:19,079
但这是个道德问题
But this is a moral argument.

131
00:08:19,251 --> 00:08:21,242
是 但即使...
Yes, but even...

132
00:08:22,251 --> 00:08:27,689
等等 我有主意了 这招也许能打败财政部
Wait a minute. I've got an idea. This could be a way to beat the Treasury.

133
00:08:27,891 --> 00:08:31,247
您是说您会支持我?     你说得有理
You mean you'll support me? You've made your point.

134
00:08:31,411 --> 00:08:34,926
值得一试 我甚至会看你的报告...再看一遍
We'll give it a try. I'll even read your report. Again!

135
00:08:37,131 --> 00:08:40,680
这会非常有趣 十分感谢你
This could be very interesting. Thank you very much indeed.

136
00:08:40,891 --> 00:08:43,280
但您会支持我吗?
But will you support me?

137
00:08:43,451 --> 00:08:45,726
当然 但不会公开
Yeah, well, not publicly.

138
00:08:45,891 --> 00:08:49,341
这会削弱我的分量 削弱我的说服力
It would undermine my position, undermine the argument

139
00:08:49,341 --> 00:08:51,442
如果我一开始就支持的话
if I supported you from the start.

140
00:08:51,851 --> 00:08:56,242
我必须显得中立 被论据所说服
I have to be seen as the impartial judge swayed by the force of the argument.

141
00:08:56,451 --> 00:08:58,442
对 我明白
Yes, I see that.

142
00:08:58,611 --> 00:09:02,399
但是私下里 我希望强力推进此事 强力推进
But off the record, I'd like to see this pushed very hard indeed.

143
00:09:02,571 --> 00:09:06,450
希望你发表些演说 彼得 非常感谢你
Make some speeches on it. Peter, thank you very much indeed.

144
00:09:08,931 --> 00:09:13,402
谢谢你的香烟纸...香烟报告
Thank you for your cigarette paper... your paper on cigarettes.

145
00:09:16,331 --> 00:09:18,799
您是认真的吗 首相?     什么 伯纳?
Is this serious? What do you mean?

146
00:09:19,011 --> 00:09:21,081
一贯做法是反对
It's always been the practice

147
00:09:21,251 --> 00:09:25,563
大臣们做反吸烟演说 做了的话 不印发 不推广
to discourage anti-smoking speeches by ministers and not to distribute them.

148
00:09:25,771 --> 00:09:29,684
我希望彼得的演说能印发 并推广 人人都要知道
Well, I want Peter's speeches distributed. I want everybody to know.

149
00:09:29,891 --> 00:09:33,940
是 首相 您认为您能赢吗?
Yes, Prime Minister. Do you think you will win this one?

150
00:09:33,940 --> 00:09:35,961
烟草商的游说非常有力
The tobacco lobby is very powerful.

151
00:09:35,961 --> 00:09:40,564
有赢就有输 伯纳 这次我必输无疑
Well, some you win, some you lose, Bernard. This one I shall definitely lose.

152
00:09:40,771 --> 00:09:42,284
那是为什么?
Then why?

153
00:09:42,451 --> 00:09:46,444
如果你是财政部长 你会选择减税15亿
If you were the Treasury, would you rather do without ?.5 billion in tax cuts

154
00:09:46,611 --> 00:09:48,966
还是失去40亿烟草税呢?
or ? billion in lost tobacco tax revenue?

155
00:09:49,131 --> 00:09:51,440
当然是减税
The tax cuts. (PHONE RINGS)

156
00:09:51,651 --> 00:09:55,121
就是 那就是我的目的 我一定会达成
Exactly. That's what I want and that's what I shall get.

157
00:09:55,331 --> 00:09:57,925
是汉弗莱爵士 他能来谈谈吗?     好 当然
Can Sir Humphrey have a word? Of course.

158
00:09:58,091 --> 00:10:00,161
好 请进
Yes, come in, please.

159
00:10:03,171 --> 00:10:05,560
首相      汉弗莱
Prime Minister... Humphrey.

160
00:10:05,731 --> 00:10:09,041
我在想 您和索恩博士聊得高兴吗?
Did you have an interesting chat with Dr Thorne?

161
00:10:09,251 --> 00:10:11,970
对 他提议彻底禁烟
Yes. He proposed the elimination of smoking.

162
00:10:15,811 --> 00:10:18,609
也许要通过大规模催眠吧
By a campaign of mass hypnosis perhaps!

163
00:10:19,571 --> 00:10:24,691
不 通过大幅提高烟草税 同时禁止一切广告
By raising tobacco taxes sky high and simultaneously banning all advertising.

164
00:10:27,331 --> 00:10:29,458
你不觉得他的出发点非常崇高吗?
I think his position is admirably moral.

165
00:10:29,458 --> 00:10:32,294
也许崇高 但是蠢到极点
Moral perhaps, but extremely silly.

166
00:10:32,294 --> 00:10:36,050
头脑健全的人都不会考虑这种提议
No man in his right mind could contemplate such a proposal.

167
00:10:36,251 --> 00:10:38,446
我就在考虑呢
I'm contemplating it.

168
00:10:38,611 --> 00:10:42,889
是 当然 首相 请别误会
Yes, of course, Prime Minister. Please don't misunderstand me.

169
00:10:43,051 --> 00:10:48,045
您当然要考虑您政府的所有行政提案
It is quite right that you should CONTEMPLATE all proposals

170
00:10:48,211 --> 00:10:50,679
但没有正常人会支持它
but no sane man would ever SUPPORT it.

171
00:10:50,891 --> 00:10:54,406
我就支持     这也是您应该的 首相
I'm supporting it. And quite right too, Prime Minister.

172
00:10:54,571 --> 00:11:00,043
但问题是 烟草税是政府税收主要来源
The only problem is that the tax is a major source of revenue for the government.

173
00:11:00,251 --> 00:11:02,680
也是致命疾病的主要来源
And a major source of death from diseases.

174
00:11:02,891 --> 00:11:07,009
是 但并没有任何已证实的必然联系啊
Yes, but no definite causative link has ever been proved, has it?

175
00:11:07,211 --> 00:11:10,123
但数据...     数据能证明任何事
The statistics... You can prove anything with statistics.

176
00:11:10,331 --> 00:11:12,970
甚至事实?      对...不
Even the truth. Yes... No!

177
00:11:13,171 --> 00:11:19,849
它说 "吸烟引起的疾病每年花费卫生部1.65亿"
It says here, ''Smoking-related diseases cost the NHS ?65 million a year.''

178
00:11:20,051 --> 00:11:22,440
是 但我们调查过
Yes, but we've been into that.

179
00:11:22,611 --> 00:11:27,401
结果是 如果这10万人活下来 寿终正寝
It has been shown that if those extra 100,000 people had lived to a ripe old age,

180
00:11:27,571 --> 00:11:31,803
他们需要的养老金和社会保障金
they would have cost us even more in pensions and social security

181
00:11:31,971 --> 00:11:34,439
比医疗费还要多
than they did in medical treatment.

182
00:11:34,611 --> 00:11:37,887
所以从财政角度说 毫无疑问
So financially speaking, it's unquestionably better

183
00:11:38,051 --> 00:11:41,248
保持现有的死亡率再好不过了
that they continue to die at about the present rate.

184
00:11:42,691 --> 00:11:45,298
1833年 霍乱造成3万人死亡
''When cholera killed 30,000 people in 1833,

185
00:11:45,298 --> 00:11:46,919
我们得到公共卫生法案
we got the Public Health Act.

186
00:11:46,919 --> 00:11:49,636
1952年 工业废气造成2500人死亡
''When smog killed 2,500 people in 1952,

187
00:11:49,636 --> 00:11:51,594
我们得到空气净化法案
we got the Clean Air Act.''

188
00:11:51,594 --> 00:11:54,487
一种商业药物造成6人死亡
A commercial drug kills half a dozen people

189
00:11:54,487 --> 00:11:56,301
我们禁止它出售
and we get it withdrawn from sale.

190
00:11:56,331 --> 00:12:00,244
香烟每年杀死10万人 我们得到什么?
Cigarettes kill 100,000 people a year and what do we get?

191
00:12:00,451 --> 00:12:03,090
40亿岁入
? billion a year.

192
00:12:03,291 --> 00:12:07,762
25000个烟草业工作岗位 出口业蓬勃发展
25,000 jobs in the tobacco industry, a flourishing cigarette export business,

193
00:12:07,931 --> 00:12:10,286
有效平衡了贸易额
helping our balance of trade,

194
00:12:10,451 --> 00:12:14,364
25000个岗位涵盖零售 包装 贸易诸多领域
250,000 jobs related to tobacco newsagents, packaging, transport...

195
00:12:14,571 --> 00:12:16,334
这些数据只是估计而已
These figures are just guesses.

196
00:12:16,334 --> 00:12:19,278
不 这是政府数...是事实
No, they're government st... They're facts.

197
00:12:21,451 --> 00:12:25,205
好 你的数据是事实 而我的事实只是数据?
So your statistics are facts and my facts are merely statistics?

198
00:12:25,411 --> 00:12:27,192
首相 我站在您这边
I'm on your side.

199
00:12:27,192 --> 00:12:30,440
我只是指出一些您会碰到的争论
I'm merely giving you some arguments you'll encounter.

200
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:33,690
谢谢 汉弗莱 真高兴连你都支持
Humphrey, I'm so glad to know we'll have support such as yours.

201
00:12:33,851 --> 00:12:36,027
可首相 会有人指出
It will be pointed out that the

202
00:12:36,027 --> 00:12:38,580
烟草公司是体育的重要赞助商
tobacco companies are great sponsors of sport.

203
00:12:38,580 --> 00:12:43,087
一旦BBC的体育直播节目没有烟草广告...
Where would the BBC sports programmes be if cigarette companies couldn't advert...

204
00:12:43,291 --> 00:12:46,363
没有烟草公司赞助 会怎样呢?
couldn't SPONSOR the events that they televise?

205
00:12:47,451 --> 00:12:49,919
汉弗莱 我们在讨论每年10万人的死亡
We're talking about 100,000 deaths a year.

206
00:12:50,131 --> 00:12:54,727
对 但烟草税占了公共卫生资金的1/3
Yes, but cigarette taxes pay for a third of the cost of the National Health Service.

207
00:12:54,891 --> 00:12:58,088
我们多挽救了这么多生命
We're saving many more lives than we otherwise could

208
00:12:58,251 --> 00:13:00,330
因为这些烟民自愿
because of those smokers who voluntarily

209
00:13:00,330 --> 00:13:02,003
为挽救同胞们牺牲了自己
lay down their lives for their friends.

210
00:13:04,011 --> 00:13:06,479
烟民是我们国家的恩人啊
Smokers are national benefactors.

211
00:13:07,611 --> 00:13:09,602
只要他们活着
So long as they live!

212
00:13:09,771 --> 00:13:12,922
吸烟和死亡的关系从未被证实 我说过了
Not that any definite causal link has ever been proved.

213
00:13:13,131 --> 00:13:15,580
首相 内阁会议要开始了
It's time for your next Cabinet committee,

214
00:13:15,580 --> 00:13:19,366
午餐安排在下院 体育大臣有急事找您
then the Minister of Sport wants an urgent word.

215
00:13:19,366 --> 00:13:21,519
关于什么?      赞助
What about? Sponsorship.

216
00:13:22,731 --> 00:13:26,280
谁向他告的密?他是烟草业的说客
Who tipped him off? He's one of the tobacco lobby.

217
00:13:26,491 --> 00:13:29,164
是您政府中的一员
A member of YOUR government?

218
00:13:29,331 --> 00:13:32,145
对 他是体育大臣 有既得利益
Yes, he's Minister for Sport. He has a vested interest.

219
00:13:32,145 --> 00:13:34,430
还是诺丁汉的议员
He's also an MP for Nottingham.

220
00:13:34,430 --> 00:13:36,879
你告诉他的? 他怎么会知道?
Did you tell him? How did he know?

221
00:13:37,051 --> 00:13:39,565
小道消息 首相
The grapevine perhaps. Prime Minister...

222
00:13:40,611 --> 00:13:43,125
告诉他 我2点半在下院见他10分钟
Tell the minister I'll see him at 2.30.

223
00:13:43,291 --> 00:13:47,762
好的 首相      不好 伯纳 不过我是逃不掉了
With pleasure, Prime Minister. Not with pleasure, but I'll see him anyway.

224
00:13:49,291 --> 00:13:51,759
首相 体育大臣来了
The Minister for Sport, Prime Minister.

225
00:13:51,931 --> 00:13:54,525
莱斯利 亲爱的朋友 你好
Oh, Leslie, my dear fellow. Hi.

226
00:13:57,011 --> 00:13:59,479
您介意我抽烟吗?
Do you mind if I smoke?

227
00:14:01,211 --> 00:14:03,725
首相 有个流言
Prime Minister, it's about the rumour

228
00:14:03,891 --> 00:14:07,964
说您本人打算攻击烟草业
that you intend to make a personal attack on the tobacco industry.

229
00:14:08,131 --> 00:14:10,725
我没听说啊      您是说是假的?
I hadn't heard that rumour. It's not true?

230
00:14:10,891 --> 00:14:13,928
卫生部大臣正有此意 但没人打算付诸实践
The Minister for Health is considering the matter.

231
00:14:14,091 --> 00:14:16,480
无火不起烟
There's no smoke without fire.

232
00:14:16,651 --> 00:14:20,724
会和你商议的 作为体育大臣 你有即得利益
You'd be consulted. As Minister for Sport, you have an interest.

233
00:14:20,931 --> 00:14:22,922
别提什么体育
Never mind sport.

234
00:14:23,091 --> 00:14:26,814
我有边缘选区在布里斯托尔 诺丁汉
There are marginal seats in Bristol, Nottingham,

235
00:14:26,814 --> 00:14:29,871
格拉斯哥 巴塞尔顿和北爱尔兰
Glasgow, Basildon and Northern Ireland,

236
00:14:29,871 --> 00:14:31,366
都是烟草工人的票
all with tobacco workers.

237
00:14:31,531 --> 00:14:35,809
我选区里有4千烟草工人 我的席位怎么办?
I've got 4,000 tobacco workers in my constituency. What about my seat?

238
00:14:39,011 --> 00:14:41,127
你的肺怎样?
What about your lungs?

239
00:14:41,651 --> 00:14:43,642
我的肺好得很
My lungs are fine.

240
00:14:43,851 --> 00:14:46,604
他不是用屁股(席位)来呼吸的
He doesn't breathe through his seat.

241
00:14:48,131 --> 00:14:50,725
哦 席位 我懂了 抱歉
Oh, your seat, I see, I'm sorry.

242
00:14:50,891 --> 00:14:52,828
谢谢 伯纳 我知道你的难处
Thank you, Bernard. I see the difficulty,

243
00:14:52,828 --> 00:14:54,479
但只要符合国家利益
but if something is right for the country,

244
00:14:55,691 --> 00:14:58,159
无疑 政府必须去做
surely the government must pursue it.

245
00:14:58,331 --> 00:15:03,121
政府当然得做正确的事 只要不影响边缘选区
The government must do what's right, but not if it affects marginal constituencies.

246
00:15:03,291 --> 00:15:06,044
这得有个限度      目前还没有下决定
There is a limit. No decision has been taken.

247
00:15:06,251 --> 00:15:08,924
为了我们党的利益 你也不能这么做
For the good of the party, you can't do this.

248
00:15:09,131 --> 00:15:13,124
你不是英国烟草集团聘的顾问吗?
Weren't you a paid consultant to the British Tobacco Group?

249
00:15:13,891 --> 00:15:18,521
当然 英国烟草集团是给过我一丁点聘金
Of course, the fact that the BTG did pay me a small retainer,

250
00:15:18,691 --> 00:15:21,080
这完全跑题了嘛
it's totally beside the point.

251
00:15:21,251 --> 00:15:26,769
他们是非常慷慨的组织 有强烈的社会责任感
They're a very generous corporation with a strong sense of responsibility

252
00:15:26,931 --> 00:15:29,525
看看他们给体育的钱吧 您还想制止他们
Look at all the money they give to sport!

253
00:15:29,731 --> 00:15:32,199
他们只是为了卖出更多的烟
They just do it to sell more cigarettes.

254
00:15:32,371 --> 00:15:35,204
不 他们把这当作是对社会的服务
No, they do it as a service to the community.

255
00:15:35,411 --> 00:15:41,043
哦 好 他们喜欢捐款就匿名捐吧
Oh, that's all right, then. They can go on giving the money anonymously if they like.

256
00:15:41,251 --> 00:15:43,719
我肯定他们会非常乐意
Well, I'm sure they'd be happy to,

257
00:15:43,891 --> 00:15:48,362
如果他们能把匿名捐款的事迹公布的话
provided they could publicise the fact that they were doing it anonymously.

258
00:15:48,531 --> 00:15:52,605
告诉我 彼得索恩是不是还想
Is it true that Peter Thorne is also trying to

259
00:15:52,605 --> 00:15:54,304
改掉政府的健康警告?
change the government health warning?

260
00:15:54,339 --> 00:15:55,130
是吗?
Is it?

261
00:15:55,291 --> 00:16:00,763
貌似他提议改成"死于肺癌严重影响健康"
He's proposing something like ''Dying of lung cancer can seriously damage your health''.

262
00:16:00,971 --> 00:16:02,962
这是撒谎
It is not true!

263
00:16:03,131 --> 00:16:05,599
如果我们袖手旁观 在未来10年内
If we do nothing, in the next ten years,

264
00:16:05,771 --> 00:16:08,922
我们一个国家 就会有100万人英年早逝
in this country we'll have one million premature deaths.

265
00:16:09,131 --> 00:16:11,599
是 但却分布均匀
Yes, but evenly spread.

266
00:16:12,971 --> 00:16:15,485
不局限在边缘选区里
Not just in marginal constituencies.

267
00:16:16,131 --> 00:16:21,046
听着 吉姆 还没有任何有效证据表明
Listen, Jim, there is no conclusive proof of any causal link

268
00:16:21,211 --> 00:16:23,361
是吸烟导致了...
between smoking and...

269
00:16:27,131 --> 00:16:30,840
我们卫生部真的非常关心吸烟问题
We at the DHSS are profoundly worried about smoking.

270
00:16:31,051 --> 00:16:35,522
我们的确有责任帮首相达成目标
And we agree it's our duty to help the Prime Minister achieve his objective,

271
00:16:35,691 --> 00:16:38,113
但鉴于1/3选民都吸烟
but with a third of the voters as smokers,

272
00:16:38,113 --> 00:16:39,682
我也不能把税抬得太高
I can't raise taxes too high.

273
00:16:40,251 --> 00:16:43,596
一来 大臣不会在选票上自寻死路
The Chancellor won't commit electoral suicide

274
00:16:43,596 --> 00:16:46,436
二来 通货膨胀也要考虑
and the inflationary effect is considerable.

275
00:16:46,436 --> 00:16:48,565
但得承认 这事关道德原则
There is a moral principle involved.

276
00:16:48,771 --> 00:16:50,887
道德原则 对
Moral principle, yes.

277
00:16:51,091 --> 00:16:54,337
我们理解并支持首相的担心
We understand the PM's concern.

278
00:16:54,337 --> 00:16:57,523
事实上 我们也相信道德原则
In fact, we earnestly believe in the moral principle.

279
00:16:57,523 --> 00:17:01,044
但当关系到40亿税收
But where ? billion of revenue is at stake,

280
00:17:01,211 --> 00:17:04,203
我想我们得极其慎重地考虑
I think we should have to consider very carefully

281
00:17:04,371 --> 00:17:06,885
我们是否有权纵容自己
whether we have the right to indulge ourselves

282
00:17:07,051 --> 00:17:11,203
自私地一味满足对道德的追求
in the rather selfish luxury of pursuing moral principles.

283
00:17:11,411 --> 00:17:14,863
没有烟草商赞助 艺术怎么办呢?
Where would the arts be without tobacco sponsorship?

284
00:17:14,863 --> 00:17:17,275
不是得靠艺术委员会了
At the mercy of the Arts Council.

285
00:17:17,275 --> 00:17:20,630
可不是 那些愚蠢的压力集团
Exactly. Then those silly pressure groups and

286
00:17:20,630 --> 00:17:22,705
狂热分子 像皇家内科医师协会
fanatics like the Royal College of Physicians!

287
00:17:22,740 --> 00:17:24,002
狂热分子
Fanatics!

288
00:17:24,171 --> 00:17:27,163
竟然奢想政府出台干预政策
They want the government to have a policy on the matter.

289
00:17:27,371 --> 00:17:30,363
如果政府是一支团队 情况会不同
It would be different if the government were a team,

290
00:17:30,531 --> 00:17:34,001
可惜实际上 它是敌对部落结成松散联邦体
but in fact they're a loose confederation of warring tribes.

291
00:17:35,251 --> 00:17:38,923
要是首相见过烟草商
If only the PM could meet the tobacco people,

292
00:17:38,923 --> 00:17:41,903
就会知道 他们都是多好的人啊
he could see what really nice chaps they were.

293
00:17:41,903 --> 00:17:44,528
而且非常关心人民健康问题
And genuinely concerned about the health risks.

294
00:17:44,731 --> 00:17:47,939
他们不可能有什么不对
There can't be anything wrong with them.

295
00:17:47,939 --> 00:17:51,209
烟草集团理事会还有一位前常任秘书呢
BTG have an ex-Permanent Secretary on their board.

296
00:17:51,209 --> 00:17:54,684
还能接纳更多      时机成熟的时候
And could well have more. In the fullness of time.

297
00:17:55,691 --> 00:17:59,923
我觉得问题出在你们大臣本身 伊安
I think we ought to raise some questions about your minister, Ian.

298
00:18:00,091 --> 00:18:03,970
对这个问题他懂什么? 索恩只是个医生
What does he know about the subject? Peter Thorne is only a doctor.

299
00:18:04,131 --> 00:18:06,645
他唯一的目的就是让人活着
His sole purpose is keeping people alive!

300
00:18:06,851 --> 00:18:08,842
偏见太重
Must be biased.

301
00:18:09,011 --> 00:18:10,773
看到自己的病人死去
Seeing your patients die

302
00:18:10,773 --> 00:18:13,313
一定从情绪上影响他的判断力
must emotionally distort your judgement.

303
00:18:13,651 --> 00:18:18,406
完全可以理解 但感情用事是决策的大忌
It's very understandable, but a great handicap to cool decision-taking.

304
00:18:18,611 --> 00:18:21,887
太对了 但找不出更有力的说辞吗?
Very true, but can we find something a bit stronger?

305
00:18:22,091 --> 00:18:26,482
弗兰克 我想关键在于 我们生活在自由国家
Frank, I think the crucial argument is that we're living in a free country.

306
00:18:26,651 --> 00:18:29,165
我们必须有权为自己作主
We must be free to make our own decisions.

307
00:18:29,331 --> 00:18:33,324
不能把政府当保姆 我们可不想要个奶妈政府
Government shouldn't be a nursemaid. We don't want the nanny state.

308
00:18:33,491 --> 00:18:34,844
好      好极了
Very good. Excellent.

309
00:18:35,011 --> 00:18:38,162
唯一的问题是 这个说法
The only problem is that is also the argument

310
00:18:38,331 --> 00:18:40,339
也被用来宣传大麻 海洛因 砒霜
for legalising the sale of marijuana, heroin

311
00:18:40,339 --> 00:18:42,232
和硝化甘油合法化
arsenic and gelignite.

312
00:18:42,291 --> 00:18:45,920
也许为它们课重税 也不失为一个好主意
Maybe that's a good idea if we put a big enough tax on them.

313
00:18:46,131 --> 00:18:49,043
从政治上讲很难      太可惜了
Politically difficult. Pity.

314
00:18:49,251 --> 00:18:50,730
是啊
Yes.

315
00:18:51,971 --> 00:18:53,484
有了
Got it!

316
00:18:54,611 --> 00:18:58,968
首相当年还是行政大臣的时候
When the Prime Minister was Minister for Administrative Affairs,

317
00:18:59,131 --> 00:19:04,569
我常拉他去上院 温布尔登和格林徳堡歌剧院
I used to get him to accompany me on regular visits to Wimbledon Glyndebourne

318
00:19:04,771 --> 00:19:06,966
去做烟草协会的贵宾
as a guest of BTG,

319
00:19:07,131 --> 00:19:12,410
他可受了烟草商盛情款待 招待费少说上百
so he's thoroughly implicated in receiving hospitality worth hundreds,

320
00:19:12,571 --> 00:19:14,960
甚至上千
possibly thousands from them.

321
00:19:15,131 --> 00:19:20,046
如果把这消息漏出去 会多么轰动
Now, if that were to leak... shocking though a leak would be...

322
00:19:20,211 --> 00:19:23,123
哦 是够轰动的      轰动
Oh, shocking. Shocking.

323
00:19:23,851 --> 00:19:27,446
首相的处境一定会非常尴尬
It'd be profoundly embarrassing for the Prime Minister.

324
00:19:27,611 --> 00:19:30,444
真搞不懂我怎么没早想到呢
I can't think why I didn't think of it before.

325
00:19:30,611 --> 00:19:32,602
我也搞不懂
Nor can I.

326
00:19:36,651 --> 00:19:39,119
好啊 伯纳      是 首相
Well, Bernard. Well, Prime Minister.

327
00:19:39,331 --> 00:19:41,891
很好 伯纳 事情进展非常顺利
Very well. Things are going very well indeed.

328
00:19:42,091 --> 00:19:44,082
好事啊
Oh, good.

329
00:19:44,251 --> 00:19:47,243
我让财政部走投无路了 还有财政大臣
I've got the Treasury on the run and the Chancellor.

330
00:19:47,411 --> 00:19:49,879
这好吗? 他可是您政府的一员
Is that good? He's in your own government.

331
00:19:50,051 --> 00:19:55,079
当然好 他们得学会听话 跟我合作
Of course it's good. They've got to learn to come to heel and learn to co-operate.

332
00:19:55,291 --> 00:19:59,330
您的"合作"怎么讲?      就是服从我的命令
What do you mean, co-operate? I mean obey my commands!

333
00:19:59,531 --> 00:20:01,010
我懂了
I see.

334
00:20:01,211 --> 00:20:04,726
"合作"就这个意思 当你是首相的时候
That's what ''co-operate'' means when you're Prime Minister.

335
00:20:04,891 --> 00:20:07,286
首相 您为什么非要减税呢?
Why are these tax cuts in your interest?

336
00:20:07,286 --> 00:20:10,344
我知道财政部不愿还钱 但他们也是您的政府
It's your government too.

337
00:20:10,379 --> 00:20:14,521
伯纳 很简单 减税15亿能赢得大量选票
Bernard, it's simple. Cutting taxes by ?.5 billion is going to win us masses of votes.

338
00:20:14,691 --> 00:20:18,473
我的大臣揽钱只为了自己的部门
My ministers are interested in getting money for their departments

339
00:20:18,473 --> 00:20:19,626
而不是支持我
not in supporting me.

340
00:20:19,731 --> 00:20:23,519
所以我要支持索恩 来和财政部抗衡
I'm using my support for Peter Thorne as leverage on the Treasury.

341
00:20:23,731 --> 00:20:26,450
您的忠诚支持?      没错
Your loyal support? Precisely.

342
00:20:26,611 --> 00:20:29,045
为了换他们的忠诚支持
In order to get THEIR loyal support.

343
00:20:29,211 --> 00:20:32,492
等您达成减税 是不是要收回
After you get the tax cut, you will withdraw your

344
00:20:32,492 --> 00:20:34,142
这一忠诚支持呢?
support from Peter Thorne?

345
00:20:34,142 --> 00:20:36,922
伯纳 你怎么这么世故?
Bernard, how can you be so cynical?

346
00:20:37,091 --> 00:20:39,764
我只调整一下优先级而已
I shall simply rearrange my priorities.

347
00:20:39,931 --> 00:20:42,525
汉弗莱爵士在门外等候
Sir Humphrey's waiting to see you outside.

348
00:20:42,691 --> 00:20:44,841
马上让他进来
Send him in at once.

349
00:20:45,011 --> 00:20:49,004
是 首相 您的话就是我的"合作"
Yes, Prime Minister. Your word is my co-operation.

350
00:20:54,251 --> 00:20:56,242
汉弗莱      首相大人
Humphrey! Prime Minister.

351
00:20:56,411 --> 00:20:57,710
一切都还顺利吧?
Everything all right?

352
00:20:57,710 --> 00:21:01,073
所有事 首相 恐怕都非常不顺利
Everything is very far from all right.

353
00:21:01,108 --> 00:21:04,086
出什么问题了?      您的禁烟法令
What's the trouble? Your anti-smoking legislation.

354
00:21:04,251 --> 00:21:05,684
怎么了?
What about it?

355
00:21:05,851 --> 00:21:08,888
尽管您的提议
Notwithstanding the fact that your proposal

356
00:21:09,051 --> 00:21:12,726
能够带来一些无关紧要的附加利益
could encompass certain concomitant benefits of a peripheral relevance,

357
00:21:12,891 --> 00:21:16,884
但同时恐怕会造成极其重大之至的顾虑
there is a countervailing consideration of infinitely superior magnitude,

358
00:21:17,051 --> 00:21:20,930
甚至牵扯到您的自律与渎职行为
involving your personal complicity and corroborative malfeasance,

359
00:21:21,091 --> 00:21:26,085
后果是 您从前的交情与娱乐活动的漏洞和污点
with the consequence that the taint and stigma of your former diversions

360
00:21:26,251 --> 00:21:30,005
将无可救药地 不可避免地动摇您的位置
could irredeemably and irretrievably invalidate your position

361
00:21:30,171 --> 00:21:34,961
并在公众揭发和舆论谴责下 让您难堪到极点
and culminate in public revelations and recriminations of a profoundly embarrassing

362
00:21:35,131 --> 00:21:37,645
最终毫无挽回余地
and ultimately indefensible character.

363
00:21:39,131 --> 00:21:41,599
也许你该对这番话做个总结
Perhaps I could have a pr閏is of that.

364
00:21:44,091 --> 00:21:47,640
您双手沾满尼古丁      这作何理解?
There's nicotine on your hands. What do you mean?

365
00:21:47,851 --> 00:21:51,730
烟草协会给我们的所有那些好处
All the hospitality that we've enjoyed at BTG's expense.

366
00:21:51,891 --> 00:21:54,531
香槟招待会 午餐会
Champagne receptions,

367
00:21:54,531 --> 00:21:56,105
体育比赛和文艺演出的贵宾席
the best seats at sporting and cultural events.

368
00:21:56,105 --> 00:21:58,889
有什么问题?      烟草公司可能
What's the problem?

369
00:21:58,889 --> 00:22:00,779
把这些难堪事告诉媒体
The tobacco companies may tell the press.

370
00:22:00,779 --> 00:22:03,734
难堪什么? 我在苏联大使馆喝过酒
So? I've had drinks at the Soviet embassy.

371
00:22:03,734 --> 00:22:06,025
也不能就说我是俄国间谍吧
That doesn't make me a Russian spy.

372
00:22:06,411 --> 00:22:08,925
哦...好...哦
Oh... Well... Oh.

373
00:22:10,411 --> 00:22:12,720
是不是?      好 好
Does it? Well, no.

374
00:22:12,891 --> 00:22:15,405
随他们去捣鬼吧 还有别的吗?
Let them do their worst. Anything else?

375
00:22:15,571 --> 00:22:19,928
首相 还有非常重要的一点您要切记
Well, Prime Minister, there is another vital point to bear in mind.

376
00:22:20,091 --> 00:22:22,605
许多人 赫赫有名的人物 有影响的人物
A lot of eminent people, influential people

377
00:22:22,771 --> 00:22:26,650
都争论说 这种法令是对自由选择权的侵犯
argue that such legislation would be a blow against freedom of choice.

378
00:22:26,851 --> 00:22:29,673
一派胡言 我又没禁止吸烟本身
Rubbish! I'm not banning smoking

379
00:22:29,673 --> 00:22:32,966
难道每次加税就是对自由的剥夺?
Does every tax rise represent a blow against freedom?

380
00:22:33,001 --> 00:22:34,719
这要取决于税加了多少
Well, it depends how big the tax rise is.

381
00:22:35,491 --> 00:22:38,563
好极了 20便士算剥夺自由了吗?
Fascinating! Does 20 pence represent a blow against freedom?

382
00:22:38,771 --> 00:22:42,764
首相      25? 30便士? 31?
Prime Minister... 25 pence? 30 pence? 31?

383
00:22:42,931 --> 00:22:48,005
只要严重损害你利益 就是破坏自由吗?
Is something a blow against freedom because it can seriously damage your wealth?

384
00:22:48,211 --> 00:22:51,098
首相 我得警告您会有阻碍
I must warn you of the difficulties.

385
00:22:51,098 --> 00:22:54,174
我预见到种种不可预见的问题
I foresee all sorts of unforeseen problems.

386
00:22:54,174 --> 00:22:55,123
比如?
Such as?

387
00:22:55,291 --> 00:22:58,488
如果我能预见 那还叫不可预见的问题吗?
If I could foresee them, they wouldn't be unforeseen.

388
00:23:00,651 --> 00:23:03,370
但你刚刚说你可以预见啊
You just said you COULD foresee them.

389
00:23:03,531 --> 00:23:06,523
首相 如果发起部际委员会 议会调查
If we could set up an inter-departmental committee,

390
00:23:06,691 --> 00:23:10,127
皇家调查委员会 或者财政部调查组
a Royal Commission, perhaps a Treasury Committee...

391
00:23:10,331 --> 00:23:13,323
别和我谈财政部      为什么?
Don't talk to me about the Treasury! Why not?

392
00:23:13,491 --> 00:23:17,484
他们为了15亿 就企图阻止我的减税计划
The Treasury are blocking my plans for a ?.5 billion tax cut.

393
00:23:18,251 --> 00:23:21,607
要是他们能...灵活些
If only they could be more...flexible.

394
00:23:28,011 --> 00:23:32,562
我觉得 他们还没认真研究过这事
Well, I don't think they're fully committed on that other matter yet.

395
00:23:32,771 --> 00:23:34,284
是吗?
Really?

396
00:23:35,371 --> 00:23:39,000
当然没有 灵活? 我肯定他们能找到办法
Absolutely not. Oh, no, I'm sure they could find a way.

397
00:23:39,211 --> 00:23:41,202
他们行吗?
Could they?

398
00:23:41,371 --> 00:23:45,887
唯一的绊脚石 就是您的禁烟令一旦通过
The only stumbling block would be if your anti-smoking proposals went through,

399
00:23:46,051 --> 00:23:50,203
他们减了这个 别的地方就减不了了
they'd be too busy with those to find a way to help with the other cuts.

400
00:23:50,411 --> 00:23:54,484
当然 我的禁烟令本身很重要
Well, of course, my anti-smoking proposals, important though they are,

401
00:23:54,651 --> 00:23:58,200
但在国防面前 恐怕就微不足道了
don't have nearly such a high priority as defence.

402
00:24:01,211 --> 00:24:03,679
卫生大臣来了首相
The Minister of State for Health is here.

403
00:24:03,851 --> 00:24:08,845
首相 请允许我去打几个电话 多谢
Prime Minister, if I might have one or two minutes to make some phone calls. Thank you.

404
00:24:09,011 --> 00:24:11,081
带他进来 伯纳
Show him in, Bernard.

405
00:24:12,371 --> 00:24:15,568
索恩博士      彼得 我能为你做什么?
Dr Thorne. Peter, what can I do for you?

406
00:24:15,731 --> 00:24:18,199
我得到些激动人心的消息
I've just had some very exciting news.

407
00:24:18,371 --> 00:24:21,268
我们得到了英国医学会 皇家内科学会
We've got full backing from the BMA

408
00:24:21,268 --> 00:24:23,732
和8个顶级医学院校的全力支持
and eight top scientific and medical colleges.

409
00:24:24,491 --> 00:24:26,482
棒极了
Marvellous.

410
00:24:27,211 --> 00:24:30,203
但你的法案不可能马上通过
But your legislation can't be put through immediately.

411
00:24:30,411 --> 00:24:34,457
当然 但在3个月内要宣布为政府政策
It is announced as government policy within three months

412
00:24:34,457 --> 00:24:36,777
一年内发布白皮书 时间挺充裕的
And a white paper in 1 year

413
00:24:36,777 --> 00:24:41,803
是 说到这 我遇到了一些困难 财政部 你知道的
Yes, since we spoke, I've encountered a few problems. The Treasury, you know.

414
00:24:42,011 --> 00:24:46,209
还有您没预料到的吗?      对 我是说不...是的
Can't be anything you didn't know already? Yes. I mean no... Well, yes.

415
00:24:46,371 --> 00:24:48,885
彼得 这不是你想象的那么简单
Peter, it's not as simple as you think.

416
00:24:49,051 --> 00:24:51,519
吉姆 我真的非常重视这个
Jim, I really am serious about this.

417
00:24:51,691 --> 00:24:54,678
这是唯一一件我政治生涯中能做到的
It's the one really important and worthwhile thing

418
00:24:54,678 --> 00:24:56,371
重要的 值得的事情
I believe I can do in politics.

419
00:24:56,406 --> 00:25:00,728
如果你阻碍它 我只有辞职 并公布原因
If you stall it, I'll have to resign. And say why.

420
00:25:00,931 --> 00:25:05,721
对不起 首相 汉弗莱爵士有急事找您
Excuse me, Prime Minister. Could Sir Humphrey see you urgently just for a moment?

421
00:25:05,891 --> 00:25:08,883
你能在外面等等吗 彼得?      好的
Would you mind waiting outside, Peter? Of course.

422
00:25:12,171 --> 00:25:14,526
首相 事情非常顺利
Prime Minister, it's quite all right.

423
00:25:14,691 --> 00:25:17,364
财政部再度审阅了您的提案
The Treasury have looked at your proposal again

424
00:25:17,364 --> 00:25:20,240
他们同意减税了
and they can encompass your tax cut,

425
00:25:20,240 --> 00:25:23,321
但前提是禁烟令到此为止
provided no work is needed on the anti-smoking proposal.

426
00:25:23,531 --> 00:25:26,045
好 汉弗莱 但我又有麻烦了
That's fine, but there is another complication.

427
00:25:26,211 --> 00:25:28,679
彼得索恩说我取消禁烟 他就辞职
Peter Thorne is going to resign if I drop it,

428
00:25:28,851 --> 00:25:33,367
向媒体告状 让我被全国医生和科学家谴责
go to the press and have me condemned by all the doctors and scientists in Britain.

429
00:25:35,171 --> 00:25:36,650
救命啊
Help!

430
00:25:39,251 --> 00:25:42,561
您在财政部不是还有一个空位吗?
You still have that government vacancy in the Treasury?

431
00:25:43,291 --> 00:25:47,603
你是说...这可是破格提拔 连升三级
You mean...? It's a very big promotion, a very rapid one.

432
00:25:47,811 --> 00:25:50,530
算不了什么 对这么能干的大臣来说
Nevertheless, for a very able minister.

433
00:25:51,731 --> 00:25:56,202
伯纳 让彼得进来 然后把环境大臣叫来
Bernard, get Peter back in here and then get on to the Department of the Environment.

434
00:25:56,371 --> 00:25:58,805
体育大臣还在的话 一起叫来
Get Leslie Potts over here at once.

435
00:25:58,971 --> 00:26:02,759
首相 我还是先...您别介意
Prime Minister, I think I'll just, erm... If you'll excuse me.

436
00:26:02,931 --> 00:26:04,922
索恩博士
Dr Thorne.

437
00:26:06,051 --> 00:26:10,647
彼得 我刚想到 我们在财政部还有个空位
Peter, I've just remembered we still have that vacancy at the Treasury.

438
00:26:10,811 --> 00:26:13,325
我绞尽脑汁想找人填补
I've been racking my brains how to fill it,

439
00:26:13,491 --> 00:26:16,767
而你这份报告 我得说 让人过目难忘
but your work on this paper has impressed me enormously.

440
00:26:16,971 --> 00:26:19,439
你不是想打发掉我吧?
You're not trying to get rid of me?

441
00:26:19,611 --> 00:26:22,409
当然不是 恰恰相反
Definitely not. Quite the reverse.

442
00:26:22,611 --> 00:26:24,602
这可是大提拔啊
It's a terrific step up.

443
00:26:24,811 --> 00:26:27,200
你应得的 你完全能胜任
But thoroughly merited.

444
00:26:27,411 --> 00:26:30,369
如果要放弃禁烟案的话 我怎能接受呢?
How can I take it if it means dropping my bill?

445
00:26:30,571 --> 00:26:33,085
彼得 坐下
Peter, sit down.

446
00:26:33,291 --> 00:26:35,930
我跟你开诚布公地说
Let me be absolutely honest with you.

447
00:26:37,851 --> 00:26:43,323
这项法案可能...肯定会很难通过
This legislation would have been...would be... will be very difficult to get through.

448
00:26:43,931 --> 00:26:47,924
财政部是最大的障碍 而不是卫生部
The Treasury is the stumbling block, not the Department of Health.

449
00:26:48,091 --> 00:26:51,606
会花很久 但如果你深入内部 弄清内幕
It'll take longer, but if you were inside learning the ropes,

450
00:26:51,771 --> 00:26:53,298
我们会有更大可能
we'd have a much better chance of

451
00:26:53,298 --> 00:26:56,989
制订一项万无一失的法案 载入史册
a watertight, foolproof Act when it gets to the statute book.

452
00:26:57,211 --> 00:27:00,487
相信我      这么说我提案没被撤销?
Believe me. So my proposals aren't dropped?

453
00:27:01,171 --> 00:27:03,480
当然没有
Absolutely not.

454
00:27:04,091 --> 00:27:07,481
好 那我接受财政部的差事      好极了
OK. I'll take the Treasury job. Good.

455
00:27:07,691 --> 00:27:10,285
太感谢了 再见 首相
Thanks a lot. Goodbye, Prime Minister.

456
00:27:15,771 --> 00:27:19,764
这下卫生部又有个空位了 现在...
That leaves us with a vacancy at the Department of Health. Now...

457
00:27:19,931 --> 00:27:22,445
体育大臣来了 首相
The Minister for Sport is here, Prime Minister.

458
00:27:24,131 --> 00:27:26,520
进来      帕兹先生
Come in. Mr Potts!

459
00:27:27,011 --> 00:27:29,445
莱斯利 我亲爱的朋友
Leslie! My dear chap.

460
00:27:30,811 --> 00:27:33,325
请坐 好
Sit down. Now...

461
00:27:34,451 --> 00:27:37,648
由你来做卫生大臣 你意下如何?
How would you like to be Minister of Health?

462
00:27:42,851 --> 00:27:45,365
我?      是的
Me? Yes.

463
00:27:46,051 --> 00:27:47,450
这个...
Well...

464
00:27:47,611 --> 00:27:50,330
这可是个大提拔啊
It's a considerable promotion.

465
00:27:50,491 --> 00:27:52,721
你应得的 你完全能胜任
But thoroughly merited.

466
00:27:53,571 --> 00:27:55,532
你非常适合这份工作
You're very suitable for the job.

467
00:27:55,532 --> 00:27:59,138
你可不是那种医学说客 不像索恩博士
You're not one of the medical lobby like Dr Peter Thorne.

468
00:27:59,811 --> 00:28:04,327
好 那我恭敬不如从命 谢谢 首相
Well, of course I can't refuse it. Thank you, Prime Minister.

469
00:28:05,171 --> 00:28:07,765
汉弗莱 见见我们新任卫生大臣
Humphrey, meet our new Minister for Health.

470
00:28:07,931 --> 00:28:10,286
哦 恭喜恭喜
Oh, congratulations.

471
00:28:11,731 --> 00:28:15,041
但如果要和烟草业对着干 我坚决拒绝
I don't want the job if it means attacking the tobacco industry.

472
00:28:15,251 --> 00:28:17,242
绝对不会
Ah, but it wouldn't.

473
00:28:17,411 --> 00:28:21,040
你看 莱斯利 我们政府官员必须得现实
You see, Leslie, we in government have to be realists.

474
00:28:21,211 --> 00:28:24,328
我希望你配合烟草业工作
I want you to work WITH the tobacco industry.

475
00:28:24,491 --> 00:28:27,005
他们真的很想解决问题
They're only trying to sort out the problems.

476
00:28:27,171 --> 00:28:30,038
他们有很多资源 人也不错
They've got huge resources, nice chaps,

477
00:28:30,038 --> 00:28:33,198
很人道主义 职员素质也高
caring people and really fabulous employers.

478
00:28:33,531 --> 00:28:35,920
他们真的在出力
They are really trying to help.

479
00:28:36,091 --> 00:28:39,686
我希望你和他们一起干 而不是对着干
I want you to work with the industry, not against it.

480
00:28:40,411 --> 00:28:42,800
好不好?
All right?

481
00:28:45,491 --> 00:28:47,482
他说什么?
What did he say?

482
00:28:47,651 --> 00:28:50,119
我想他在说 "是 首相"
I think he said, ''Yes, Prime Minister.''

483
00:28:53,205 --> 00:29:05,470
